   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2) Numerical Encoding (Matthew)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea282f1c-4f56-4d10-b306-a82d32cc58af",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Cast star_rating from String to Integer for numerical processing. (Just in case we calculate the mean or so)\n",
    "- Apply StringIndexer to encode categorical variables (verified_purchase, vine) into binary (0/1)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "ea7d6682-7bc8-48fb-ab32-c8c706bf4d18",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def cleansing2(df):\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"star_rating\", col(\"star_rating\").cast(\"int\"))\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"review_headline_length\", length(col(\"review_headline\")))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    indexer_vp = StringIndexer(inputCol=\"verified_purchase\", outputCol=\"verified_purchase_idx\", handleInvalid=\"keep\")\n",
    "    df = indexer_vp.fit(df).transform(df)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    category_indexer = StringIndexer(\n",
    "        inputCol=\"product_category\", outputCol=\"category_idx\", handleInvalid=\"keep\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    df = category_indexer.fit(df).transform(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "557f76a5-d787-4cc0-b40b-cb2e1892cb58",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3) Text Analytics & Scaling (Hana)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a95df4e0-dfc1-42c1-8b87-d3b8380f3edc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Compute review_length using the length() function on the review_body column.\n",
    "- Implement StandardScaler or MinMaxScaler to normalize numerical features for better model convergence.\n",
    "- (Optional) Prepare a Tokenizer for potential text-based model expansion in Milestone 4."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "698fe31d-bb0a-4261-997a-097f8da329b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.ml.feature import MinMaxScaler, Tokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "def cleansing3(df):\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"review_length\", length(col(\"review_body\")))\n",
    "    # numeric_cols = [\"star_rating\", \"helpful_votes\", \"total_votes\", \"review_length\"]\n",
    "    # assembler = VectorAssembler(inputCols=numeric_cols, outputCol=\"numeric_features\", handleInvalid=\"skip\")\n",
    "    # df = assembler.transform(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # scaler = MinMaxScaler(inputCol=\"numeric_features\", outputCol=\"scaled_features\")\n",
    "    # df = scaler.fit(df).transform(df)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    tokenizer = Tokenizer(inputCol=\"review_body\", outputCol=\"review_tokens\")\n",
    "    df = tokenizer.transform(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "de7e62a2-f86d-4fd7-b33b-e79504877f27",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4) Target Engineering & Sampling (Kayla)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7d936f23-e7ad-4710-bf00-5004c9b41902",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Calculate the target variable: helpfulness_ratio (helpful_votes / total_votes) for rows where total_votes > 0\n",
    "- Create other new features using Spark SQL functions (log of helpful vote, log of total votes, log of review length)\n",
    "- Implement sampleBy() for Stratified Sampling to address the heavy skew toward 5-star ratings\n",
    "- Perform the final Train/Validation/Test split (e.g., 80/10/10) for model evaluation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "612c5865-6f73-45f6-a1ae-f9419bb2e90c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql.functions import when, log1p\n",
    "\n",
    "def cleansing4(df):\n",
    "    # Target variable\n",
    "    df = df.filter(col(\"total_votes\") > 0)\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"helpfulness_ratio\", col(\"helpful_votes\") / col(\"total_votes\"))\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"label\",\n",
    "        when(col(\"helpful_votes\") / col(\"total_votes\") >= 0.5, 1.0).otherwise(0.0)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    # Feature engineering using Spark SQL functions\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"log_helpful_votes\", log1p(col(\"helpful_votes\")))\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"log_total_votes\", log1p(col(\"total_votes\")))\n",
    "    df = df.withColumn(\"log_review_length\", log1p(col(\"review_length\")))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Stratified Sampling\n",
    "    fractions = {1: 0.6, 2: 1.0, 3: 0.67, 4: 0.32, 5: 0.09}\n",
    "    df = df.sampleBy(\"star_rating\", fractions=fractions, seed=42)\n",
    "    return df"
   ]
  },
